    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6010B\n\nSPONSOR: HOYLMAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act relating to granting retroactive eligibility to apply for\nenhanced Tier 3 status to former New York City police officer Mark\nRivera\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill authorizes Abigail Rivera to apply for Enhanced\nTier 3 membership in the Police Pension Fund on behalf of her late\nhusband, former NYPD officer Mark Rivera, and allows Mrs.  Rivera to\nfile for any retirement options or death benefits that would have been\navailable to Mr. Rivera if he had been a member of Enhanced Tier 3 on\nthe date of his death.\n\nSection two of the bill states that all costs pursuant to this act shall\nbe borne by the City of New York.\n\n  Section  three  of the bill includes the effective date and the fiscal\nnote.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMark Rivera was employed as a New York Police Department  Officer  until\nMarch  21,  2015,  when he passed away due to a heart attack. Mr. Rivera\nwas a Tier 3 member of the Police Pension Fund. He is  survived  by  his\nwife, Abigail Rivera, and their young son.\n\nAfter  his death, beginning on September 8, 2016, certain Tier 3 Revised\nmembers could elect to join the Tier 3 Enhanced Plan, which among  other\nthings,  extended the statutory presumptions contained in the Heart Bill\n(General Municipal Law section 207-k) to Enhanced Plan members, pursuant\nto Chapter 298 of the Laws of 2016. Tier 3 police officers became eligi-\nble to participate in the Enhanced Plan on April 10,  2017  pursuant  to\nPart  SSS  of Chapter 59 of the Laws of 2017. Had Mr. Rivera been alive,\nhe would have been eligible to apply for Enhanced Tier 3 benefits  under\nthis provision.\n\nThis  bill  would allow Mrs. Rivera to apply for Enhanced Tier 3 member-\nship in the Police Pension Fund on behalf of her late  husband,  and  to\nfile  for  any associated death benefits had Mr. Rivera been a member of\nEnhanced Tier 3 on the date of his death.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: S.6010-A (Hoylman): Passed Senate\n\n2018: S.7780 (Hoylman): Vetoed\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThe estimated financial impact of this proposal has been  calculated  as\nthe difference between the present value of (1) and (2), where:\n\n\n\n(1)  is  the  Accidental Death and SADB benefits Officer Rivera's spouse\nwould have received if the proposed legislation were  enacted  (retroac-\ntive to the date of death on March 21, 2015, and\n\n(2) is the value of the amount of ordinary death benefits already paid.\n\nBased  on  the  actuarial  assumptions and methods described herein, the\nenactment of this proposed legislation would increase the Present  Value\nof Benefits (PVFB) and the Unfunded Accrued Liability (UAL) of POLICE by\napproximately $2.3 million. This calculation does not reflect the offset\nfor a Social Security death benefit, if any, payable to Ms. Rivera.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
